# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for MEGAsync desktop.
#
# Usage (macOS/Linux, TSan-instrumented build):
#   TSAN_OPTIONS="suppressions=<repo>/tests/tsan.supp log_path=<dir>/tsan-run" ./MEGAsync
#
# Build recipe for the instrumented binary: configure a dedicated build dir with
# ENABLE_TSAN=ON plus global "-fsanitize=thread -fno-omit-frame-pointer" in
# CMAKE_{C,CXX,OBJC,OBJCXX}_FLAGS and "-fsanitize=thread" in the linker flags.
#
# POLICY: keep this file MINIMAL. Every entry must carry a justification for
# why the report is a false positive. Suppressions match by symbol, so a real
# race inside a suppressed class would be hidden too — do not add entries to
# silence reports that have not been root-caused.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SDK -> Qt event handoff via QCoreApplication::postEvent (false positive).
#
# QTMegaListener / QTMega*Listener copy the SDK event/request on an SDK worker
# thread (MegaEventPrivate / MegaRequestPrivate copies wrapped in QTMegaEvent)
# and hand it to the GUI thread with QCoreApplication::postEvent(); the GUI
# thread reads and deletes it in customEvent(). Qt guarantees the
# happens-before ordering through its event-queue mutex, but Qt itself is not
# TSan-instrumented and QBasicMutex's fast path is a bare atomic the TSan
# runtime cannot observe, so TSan sees ctor (thread A) vs read/dtor (thread B)
# with no synchronization edge. Verified against a full churn session on
# 2026-07-29: 165 reports, ~95% were this exact family; the remaining real
# races (AccountDetailsManager::mFlags, MegaSyncLogger flags) were fixed in
# code, NOT suppressed.
race:mega::QTMegaEvent
race:mega::MegaEventPrivate
race:mega::MegaRequestPrivate
race:mega::QTMegaListener::customEvent
race:mega::QTMegaRequestListener::customEvent
race:mega::QTMegaTransferListener::customEvent
race:mega::QTMegaGlobalListener::customEvent
# vptr subfamily of the same handoff (ctor/dtor vs virtual call reports whose
# racing frame is the abstract MegaEvent base constructed on the SDK thread).
race:mega::MegaEvent::MegaEvent
